{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Canonical.CertifiedModularReduction\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovOptimalTransport\n\nCanonical regular-lane optimal-transport surfaces for Bogoliubov evolution.\n\nThis file keeps to owner data already present in `CertifiedModularReduction`:\n- `Preg/Pzero` projector split,\n- regular generator `Kambient`,\n- certified support/kill laws.\n\nNo new physics axioms are introduced.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovOptimalTransport\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical\n\nsection Core\n\nvariable {E : Type*}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]\n\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => E →L[ℝ] E\n\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedRing EndH := inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedAlgebra ℝ EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : IsTopologicalRing EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : CompleteSpace EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : SMulCommClass ℝ EndH EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : IsScalarTower ℝ EndH EndH := inferInstance\n\n/--\nAlignment obstruction for the regular-lane generator against `Preg`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def alignmentObstruction\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E)) : EndH :=\n  c.Kambient * c.Preg - c.Preg * c.Kambient\n\n/--\nCertified regular-lane support implies zero alignment obstruction.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem alignmentObstruction_eq_zero\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E)) :\n    alignmentObstruction c = 0 := by\n  unfold alignmentObstruction\n  have hSupp := c.Kambient_supported_on_Preg\n  calc\n    c.Kambient * c.Preg - c.Preg * c.Kambient\n        = c.Kambient - c.Kambient := by rw [hSupp.2, hSupp.1]\n    _ = 0 := by simp\n\n/--\nOwner `χ`-obstruction for inertial-vs-curved transport regime:\nthe certified spectral/metric anomaly.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def chiObstruction\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E)) : EndH :=\n  c.anomaly\n\n/--\n`χ = 0` exactly when spectral and metric support lanes are aligned.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem chiObstruction_eq_zero_iff_alignment\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E)) :\n    chiObstruction c = 0 ↔ c.SpectralMetricAlignment := by\n  simpa [chiObstruction] using c.anomaly_vanishes_iff_alignment\n\n/--\nCurved lane (`χ ≠ 0`) is exactly non-alignment of spectral and metric supports.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem chiObstruction_ne_zero_iff_non_alignment\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E)) :\n    chiObstruction c ≠ 0 ↔ ¬ c.SpectralMetricAlignment := by\n  simpa [chiObstruction] using\n    c.curved_regular_lane_iff_non_alignment\n\n/--\nRegular-lane optimality condition for an operator flow `U`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsOptimalBogoliubovFlow\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E))\n    (U : ℝ → EndH) : Prop :=\n  ∀ t : ℝ, U t * c.Preg = c.Preg * U t\n\n/--\nInterface theorem: any flow constructor that turns `χ = 0` into commutation\nwith `Preg` yields an optimal Bogoliubov flow.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport, capstone]\ntheorem optimal_transport_of_alignment_zero\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E))\n    (U : ℝ → EndH)\n    (hFlowGenerates :\n      ∀ t : ℝ, alignmentObstruction c = 0 → U t * c.Preg = c.Preg * U t)\n    (hAlign : alignmentObstruction c = 0) :\n    IsOptimalBogoliubovFlow c U := by\n  intro t\n  exact hFlowGenerates t hAlign\n\n/--\nCanonical exponential flow generated by the regular-lane modular Hamiltonian.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def canonicalBogoliubovFlow\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E))\n    (t : ℝ) : EndH :=\n  NormedSpace.exp (t • c.Kambient)\n\n/--\nThe canonical exponential Bogoliubov flow is regular-lane optimal.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport, capstone]\ntheorem canonicalBogoliubovFlow_isOptimal\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E)) :\n    IsOptimalBogoliubovFlow c (canonicalBogoliubovFlow c) := by\n  intro t\n  have hSupp := c.Kambient_supported_on_Preg\n  have hCommKP : Commute c.Preg c.Kambient := by\n    calc\n      c.Preg * c.Kambient = c.Kambient := hSupp.1\n      _ = c.Kambient * c.Preg := by symm; exact hSupp.2\n  have hCommFlow : Commute c.Preg (NormedSpace.exp (t • c.Kambient)) := by\n    simpa using ((hCommKP.smul_right t).exp_right)\n  simpa [canonicalBogoliubovFlow] using hCommFlow.eq.symm\n\n/--\nNo defect leakage for `Preg`-invariant states under an optimal flow.\n\n`hPzeroMulPreg` is the structural split law `Pzero * Preg = 0`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport, capstone]\ntheorem no_defect_leakage_of_optimal_flow\n    (c : CertifiedModularReduction (E := E))\n    (U : ℝ → EndH)\n    (hOptimal : IsOptimalBogoliubovFlow c U)\n    (hPzeroMulPreg : c.Pzero * c.Preg = 0)\n    (v : E) (hReg : c.Preg v = v) (t : ℝ) :\n    c.Pzero (U t v) = 0 := by\n  have hCommEval : U t (c.Preg v) = c.Preg (U t v) := by\n    simpa [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply] using congrArg (fun T : EndH => T v) (hOptimal t)\n  have hRegAfter : c.Preg (U t v) = U t v := by\n    calc\n      c.Preg (U t v) = U t (c.Preg v) := by exact hCommEval.symm\n      _ = U t v := by simp [hReg]\n  calc\n    c.Pzero (U t v)\n        = c.Pzero (c.Preg (U t v)) := by rw [hRegAfter]\n    _ = (c.Pzero * c.Preg) (U t v) := by\n          simp [ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply]\n    _ = 0 := by\n          rw [hPzeroMulPreg]\n          simp\n\nend Core\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovOptimalTransport\n","mtime":1777928003332}